    "q-96739": {
      "dom_id": "step-q96739",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "The distance covered per game by a particular soccer player is uniformly distributed between $10\\,\\text{km}$\n and $13\\,\\text{km}$ inclusive. What is the probability that this player runs $12\\,\\text{km}$ or more in a randomly selected game?",
      "worked_solution": "Let $X$ represent the distance covered by the player. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U[10,13],$ and we wish to compute $P(X\\ge 12).$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U[a,b],$ then $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a}, & a\\le x\\le b \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U[10,13],$ we have the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}, & 10\\le x\\le 13 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 12) & ={\\int }_{12}^{13}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{12}^{13}\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{x}{3}|}_{12}^{13} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{3}-\\frac{12}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
