    "q-170687": {
      "dom_id": "step-q170687",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "In an online poker tournament, the maximum loss is $10$ dollars, and the maximum win is $8$ dollars. Assuming that a player's earnings are uniformly distributed between $-10$ and $8,$ what is the probability that a randomly chosen player loses between $2$ and $8$ dollars?",
      "worked_solution": "Let $X$ represent the earnings of a randomly chosen player. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U[-10,8],$ and we wish to compute $P(-8\\le X\\le -2).$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U[a,b],$ then $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a}, & a\\le x\\le b \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U[-10,8],$ we have the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{18}, & -10\\le x\\le 8 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-8\\le X\\le -2) & ={\\int }_{-8}^{-2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-8}^{-2}\\frac{1}{18}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{x}{18}|}_{-8}^{-2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{18}-(-\\frac{8}{18}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
