    "q-170689": {
      "dom_id": "step-q170689",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "The return on a risky investment can be negative (meaning that the investor loses money) or positive. Assuming that the return on a particular investment is uniformly distributed between $-7.5%$ and $12.5%$, what is the mean return of this investment?",
      "worked_solution": "Let $X$ represent the return on the investment. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U[-7.5,12.5],$ and we wish to compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U[a,b],$ then $X$ has the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{a+b}{2}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U[-7.5,12.5],$ we have the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{-7.5+12.5}{2}=2.5\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mean return on the investment is $2.5%.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
