    "q-96912": {
      "dom_id": "step-q96912",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "The distance covered by a basketball player in an official match is uniformly distributed between $3$ and $4$ km, inclusive. What is the mean distance covered per match?",
      "worked_solution": "Let $X$ represent the distance covered by a randomly chosen basketball player. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U[3,4],$ and we wish to compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U[a,b],$ then $X$ has the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{a+b}{2}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U[3,4],$ we have the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{3+4}{2}=3.5\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mean distance covered is $3.5\\,\\text{km}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-96912-a",
              "type": "math",
