    "q-96909": {
      "dom_id": "step-q96909",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "The battery duration from a full to an empty charge of a specific smartphone model is uniformly distributed between $20$ and $30$ hours, inclusive.  What is the expected duration of the smartphone battery?",
      "worked_solution": "Let $X$ represent the duration of a randomly chosen battery. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U[20,30],$ and we wish to compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U[a,b],$ then $X$ has the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{a+b}{2}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U[20,30],$ we have the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{20+30}{2}=25\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mean battery duration is $25\\,\\text{hrs}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
