    "q-96915": {
      "dom_id": "step-q96915",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "The height of water in a dam is uniformly distributed between $120$ and $195$ meters, inclusive. What is the mean height of the water?",
      "worked_solution": "Let $X$ represent the height of water in a random inspection of the dam. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U[120,195],$ and we wish to compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U[a,b],$ then $X$ has the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{a+b}{2}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U[120,195],$ we have the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{120+195}{2}=157.5\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mean height of water in the dam is $157.5\\,\\text{m}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
