    "q-96956": {
      "dom_id": "step-q96956",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "The distance covered per game by a football player in an official match is uniformly distributed between $9$ km and $12$ km, inclusive. What is the variance in the distance covered by this player?",
      "worked_solution": "Let $X$ represent the distance covered by the player. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U[9,12],$ and we wish to compute $\\text{Var}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U[a,b],$ then $X$ has the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(b-a)^{2}}{12}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U[9,12],$ we have the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(12-9)^{2}}{12}=\\frac{9}{12}=\\frac{3}{4}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the variance of the distance covered by the football player is $\\frac{3}{4}\\,{\\text{km}}^{2}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
