    "q-96950": {
      "dom_id": "step-q96950",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "A librarian has noticed that the minimum visiting time of a visitor is $0.5$ hours, whereas the maximum time is $6.5$ hours. If the visiting time is uniformly distributed, what is its variance?",
      "worked_solution": "Let $X$ represent the visiting time of a randomly chosen visitor. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U[0.5,6.5],$ and we wish to compute $\\text{Var}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U[a,b],$ then $X$ has the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(b-a)^{2}}{12}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U[0.5,6.5],$ we have the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(6.5-0.5)^{2}}{12}=\\frac{36}{12}=3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the variance  is $3\\,{\\text{hr}}^{2}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
