    "q-96953": {
      "dom_id": "step-q96953",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "A video game randomly generates an obstacle the player has to avoid. The obstacle's $x$-coordinate is uniformly distributed along a segment whose endpoints have $x$-coordinates of $16$ and $24.$ What is the variance of the $x$-coordinate of the obstacle?",
      "worked_solution": "Let $X$ represent the randomly generated $x$-coordinate of the obstacle. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U[16,24],$ and we wish to compute $\\text{Var}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U[a,b],$ then $X$ has the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(b-a)^{2}}{12}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U[16,24],$ we have the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(24-16)^{2}}{12}=\\frac{64}{12}=\\frac{16}{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the variance of the $x$-coordinate is $\\frac{16}{3}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
